cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use or discuss this work, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "A Scaling-Cancellation Principle for Chord-Based Geometric Approximations"
type: article
authors:
  - family-names: Baker
    given-names: C. Wayne
date-released: 2026-09-11
version: preprint-v2
repository-code: "https://github.com/CWBaker360/scaling-cancellation-principle"
url: "https://github.com/CWBaker360/scaling-cancellation-principle"
abstract: >-
  This paper develops a Richardson-type scaling-cancellation framework for
  chord-based geometric approximations with even-power asymptotic expansions.
  It proves the two-scale cancellation theorem, derives the unique multi-scale
  Lagrange weights, gives the surviving-error law for geometric scale nodes,
  and records the equivalent recursive fixed-base extrapolation ladder.
  Applications include polygonal approximation of pi and an explicitly cited
  ellipse-factorization input. The paper also distinguishes fixed-resolution
  order improvement from the nonlinear proportional-subtended cubic residual
  law for approximate angle division.
keywords:
  - scaling cancellation
  - Richardson extrapolation
  - chord approximation
  - polygonal approximation
  - asymptotic analysis
  - geometric N-series
  - trisection cascade
